# CALLPOOL — hourly visitor rollup.
#
# The only timer at this level of deploy/. The others live under the profile
# directories because their period is the epoch length, and getting that wrong
# is how run 2 hid a dead crank for two hours. This one has nothing to do with
# the epoch clock: it counts a calendar day of web traffic, and a calendar day
# is 24 hours on devnet, on mainnet and during a rehearsal alike.
#
# ## Hourly, though the record is daily
#
# The file is keyed by UTC date, so once a day would be enough to finish each
# day. Hourly is for the two things that only hourly gives:
#
#   * a figure on disk that is never more than an hour stale, so `--print`
#     answers "how is launch day going" without waiting for midnight;
#   * twenty-four chances to capture a day rather than one. journald has
#     already eaten three and a half days of this site's launch-week traffic
#     without reporting anything, and every hour that passes between a request
#     and its rollup is an hour it can be lost in. The re-run is exactly
#     idempotent — `mergeHistory` replaces a day's record rather than adding to
#     it — so the extra runs cost a log parse and nothing else.
#
# **Persistent=true**, unlike the hourly sampler next to it. That one refuses
# to catch up because republishing a stale estimate with a fresh timestamp is
# worse than a gap. This is the opposite case: a missed run is a day that may
# no longer be in the journal by the time anyone notices, and catching up on
# boot is the only thing that recovers it.

[Unit]
Description=CALLPOOL — roll up website visitor counts hourly
Documentation=https://github.com/AlphaArtrem/call-pool

[Timer]
OnCalendar=hourly
# Off the hour, so it is not parsing the journal at the same minute the callout
# poll and the standings sampler are working. Nothing breaks if it is — they
# share no file — but a single-core box under launch traffic has better uses
# for that minute.
RandomizedDelaySec=300
AccuracySec=1m
Persistent=true
Unit=callpool-visitor-rollup.service

[Install]
WantedBy=timers.target
